WEBVTT

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.144
Come in.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:17.379
You wished to see me.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.851
We've known each
other for how long?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.820
Approximately 20 years.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:26.256
We've served on three
starships together.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.659
I was present at your
daughter's Kolinahr.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:33.187
I consider you one
of my closest friends.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.826
And I regard you
with the same esteem.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:39.497
I've always been
honest with you,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:44.373
but you've been keeping
something from me.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.412
I don't know what you mean.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.446
Don't you?

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:51.712
It took exhaustive research,

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.276
sifting through
teraquads of data,

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:58.222
separating fact from rumor...

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.759
but eventually,
I arrived at the truth.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.295
Captain...

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.537
Happy Birthday.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:18.709
Thank you.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.211
So, it's not long

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.646
before you hit the
big three digits, hmm?

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.910
Indeed.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.884
Have you informed anyone else

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.147
of your discovery?

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.951
Don't worry, Tuvok,
my lips are sealed.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.322
Well, you're supposed
to blow out the candle.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:36.123
That is not a Vulcan custom.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.754
Humor me.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.822
Captain to the Bridge.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.932
Well?

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.368
It was a fire hazard.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.115
We're receiving
a distress call...

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.517
a small vessel on
an intercept course.

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:02.520
Life signs?

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:03.521
One.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.182
It's Ocampan.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.091
We're being hailed.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.822
Kes?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.923
Captain Janeway...

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.592
I need your help.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:20.328
Will you please give me
permission to come aboard?

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.101
Of course. What's happened?

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.611
Please, let me come aboard.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.443
Prepare the docking port.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:30.949
Tell the Doctor to stand by.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.177
Her ship is accelerating.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.617
It's on a collision course.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.620
Janeway to Kes.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:36.620
Cut your engines.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.951
You're coming in too fast.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.218
Five seconds till impact.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.452
Lock on a tractor beam.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.585
Evasive maneuvers.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.223
Hull breach on Deck 9!

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.526
Emergency force fields.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.964
Captain, a transporter

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.797
was activated
just before impact.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.359
She's beamed aboard.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.350
I'm reading bulkhead ruptures...

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.878
Deck 11, Section 17... 18... 19.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.889
Cause?

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.152
Unknown.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.955
I have located Kes.
She's moving through

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.426
those sections.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.555
She's giving off high levels
of neurogenic energy.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.930
Janeway to Kes. Kes, respond.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.234
Hull breach, Section 20.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:08.604
Force fields.
Security to Deck 11.

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.482
Force fields are not holding.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:19.177
She's approaching
Main Engineering.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.345
Bridge to Engineering.
Intruder alert.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.881
Stop where you are.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:49.745
Kes?

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.542
State your intentions.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.458
Evacuate Engineering.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.912
Warp power is fluctuating.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.279
Torres to Bridge.

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:29.344
Kes is in direct contact
with the warp core.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.821
She's drawing power

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.016
from it somehow.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.353
Shut it down.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.848
Warp power is
returning to normal.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.178
B'Elanna, report.

00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:00.185
Lieutenant Torres is dead.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:03.916
Kes has vanished.

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.031
And send Mulcahy.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.767
He's in deflector control.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.672
We'll need more power
to Junction 12-J,

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.301
and tell Harry I
want to talk to him

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:28.506
about building
a new energy grid.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.344
Lost?

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.383
No, just looking.

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:32.816
Captain Janeway suggested that

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:34.443
I get more familiar
with the ship.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.317
Well, if you have any
questions, let me know.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:37.321
Thanks.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.119
We're about to run a diagnostic

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.659
on the warp core assembly.

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.159
You can watch if you want.

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:45.493
Thanks, but I really should
be getting back to Sick Bay.

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:55.272
Computer, how long has Voyager
been in the Delta Quadrant?

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:57.969
56 days, 17 hours.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:09.015
Back so soon?

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:10.885
I thought you went
to the Airponics Bay

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:11.887
to collect herbs.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.048
I forgot something.

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.490
Ah.

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:16.884
Pyong Ko.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:18.827
Excuse me?

00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:19.830
You encouraged me

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:21.332
to choose a name,
remember?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.130
Pyong Ko was a 21st-century
surgeon who discovered

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:26.899
the genetic sequence for
inhibiting cancer cells.

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.533
It heralded a new chapter
in Earth's medical history.

00:08:29.609 --> 00:08:31.167
That's a perfect name, Doctor.

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:32.370
Hmm.

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:35.573
Then again, I'm also
considering Schweitzer,

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:36.808
Jarvik, Pasteur.

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:38.748
There are so
many options,

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:40.217
each with
its own merits.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.550
Why don't you give it
some more thought?

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:44.453
You don't have
to decide right away.

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:46.515
Of course, it's not
that I require one

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:47.820
for reasons of vanity.

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:50.863
I'm just a
hologram, after all,

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:54.764
but if I had a name
other than "Doctor"

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.802
or "Hey, you,"
it might encourage the crew

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.769
to treat me
with a little more respect.

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:03.972
Kes?

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.486
Hello?

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:28.060
Neelix?

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:54.825
You know, Neelix, if you want
to put your own stamp on it,

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:56.486
maybe you should give it
your own name,

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:57.927
like "the Greasy Neelix,"

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.726
or the, uh,
"Double Talaxian with Cheese."

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.131
Ah. It has a nice ring to it.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.225
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.600
I'll keep that in mind.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:08.265
Sweeting, what'll
it be? The usual?

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:09.706
I'm not hungry.

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:12.938
I thought that I'd bring
Captain Janeway some coffee.

00:10:13.045 --> 00:10:15.240
That's very thoughtful.

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:20.681
I'm looking forward
to tonight.

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.914
Actually, I have
a lot of work

00:10:22.989 --> 00:10:24.354
to do in Sick Bay.

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:26.391
But I already reserved
the holodeck.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:27.824
I thought we could take

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:30.088
a moonlit stroll
through the marshlands

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:31.959
of Oshionian Prime.

00:10:32.031 --> 00:10:33.726
Another time.
I promise.

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:35.096
Something wrong?

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.395
Bad morning.

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:38.835
Anything I can do?

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:40.394
I'll be fine.

00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:43.732
I'm not having
a great day, either.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.868
Nobody seems to like
today's menu.

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:48.505
I tried blaming it
on a replicator malfunction,

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:51.448
but no one
believed me.

00:10:51.517 --> 00:10:54.281
Wait. I... I think
I see something.

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:56.514
Neelix to Security.

00:10:56.589 --> 00:10:58.386
Kes's frown is losing

00:10:58.457 --> 00:11:00.152
its structural integrity.

00:11:00.226 --> 00:11:02.558
Red Alert.
I'm detecting a smile.

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:05.358
That's my Kes.

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:07.262
The coffee?

00:11:16.609 --> 00:11:18.167
That last attack
nearly cost us

00:11:18.244 --> 00:11:19.370
our impulse drives.

00:11:19.445 --> 00:11:21.140
Fortunately,
B'Elanna found a way

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:23.078
to reroute power
from the deflector.

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:25.049
A good choice
for Chief Engineer,

00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:26.550
if I do say so myself.

00:11:26.619 --> 00:11:28.177
Getting to know
your enemy.

00:11:28.254 --> 00:11:30.484
I feel like I already do.

00:11:30.556 --> 00:11:31.955
Remember the old story?

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:35.050
A man goes to Risa,
where he meets a beautiful woman

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:37.652
who invites him
for an evening of passion.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.324
He wakes up in the morning
feeling wonderful,

00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:42.731
until he discovers
he's missing a kidney.

00:11:42.802 --> 00:11:45.600
Every cadet about to go
on his first shore leave

00:11:45.671 --> 00:11:47.229
hears that cautionary tale.

00:11:47.306 --> 00:11:50.070
Doesn't seem so outrageous
anymore, does it?

00:11:50.142 --> 00:11:52.110
No, but the Vidiians are more

00:11:52.178 --> 00:11:54.772
than just
your garden-variety monsters.

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:56.974
I've been studying
their culture.

00:11:57.083 --> 00:11:59.847
They were a lot like us
before the phage.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.411
Do I detect a note of sympathy?

00:12:03.489 --> 00:12:06.947
Makes you wonder what we'd do
under the same circumstances.

00:12:08.027 --> 00:12:08.959
Come in.

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:12.054
Oh, you read my mind.

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:13.928
Vidiians?

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:15.330
I'm afraid so.

00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:17.631
We've picked up two more ships
on long-range sensors.

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:19.068
I've gone to full
tactical alert.

00:12:19.138 --> 00:12:20.366
We're taking every precaution.

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:22.168
I'm sure you'll get
us through it safely.

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:24.539
Thanks for
the vote of confidence.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:28.569
Tuvok thinks he's found a way
to penetrate their shields.

00:12:28.647 --> 00:12:32.105
The next time they attack us,
it won't be so easy.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:33.310
That's good to hear.

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:34.943
Captain to the Bridge.

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:35.952
On my way.

00:12:36.055 --> 00:12:37.454
Oops.

00:12:37.523 --> 00:12:38.455
I... I'm so clumsy.

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:39.456
I'm sorry.

00:12:39.525 --> 00:12:40.822
Don't worry about it.

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:43.794
This desk has seen
its share of coffee spills,

00:12:43.863 --> 00:12:44.852
believe me.

00:12:54.039 --> 00:12:56.132
Ensign Wildman has
an intriguing proposal.

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.539
We've been analyzing

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:00.204
the Vidiian bio-readings
from the last attack.

00:13:00.279 --> 00:13:01.405
Their immune systems

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.448
have been compromised
by the phage.

00:13:03.516 --> 00:13:05.450
We could synthesize
a neural agent

00:13:05.518 --> 00:13:08.385
that would incapacitate
them without affecting us.

00:13:08.454 --> 00:13:10.422
Might come in handy
if we're ever boarded.

00:13:10.489 --> 00:13:11.421
Exactly.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.582
Work with the Doctor.

00:13:12.658 --> 00:13:14.717
When you've got something,
find a way to deploy it

00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:16.193
through
the environmental systems.

00:13:16.262 --> 00:13:18.787
Aye, Captain.

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:31.767
The ships we detected earlier

00:13:31.844 --> 00:13:33.471
have disappeared
from our sensors.

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:34.535
Maybe we outran them.

00:13:34.613 --> 00:13:36.376
They wouldn't give
up that easily.

00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:37.938
Why would they?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:40.712
Voyager's the only organ bank
within half a parsec.

00:13:40.786 --> 00:13:42.515
We fought off
their first attacks.

00:13:42.588 --> 00:13:45.580
Now they seem content
to show up on sensors

00:13:45.658 --> 00:13:47.455
just long enough
for us to change course.

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:49.050
It's like
we're being herded somewhere.

00:13:49.128 --> 00:13:50.595
If we maintain
our present course,

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:52.893
we're gonna enter a region
filled with subspace vacuoles.

00:13:52.965 --> 00:13:54.762
We'd have to drop
to impulse to get through.

00:13:54.834 --> 00:13:56.426
Sounds like a good place
for an ambush.

00:13:56.502 --> 00:13:57.696
The Maquis used to lure

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.533
the Cardassians
into the Badlands.

00:13:59.605 --> 00:14:02.039
Those Galor-class cruisers
had nowhere to run.

00:14:02.107 --> 00:14:04.667
Neither will we, unless...

00:14:04.743 --> 00:14:08.076
Tom, how dense
are those vacuoles?

00:14:08.147 --> 00:14:11.378
They cover about 70
percent of the region.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.111
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:14:13.185 --> 00:14:15.278
Tom, what's the first thing
they teach you

00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:17.083
about maneuvering
at warp?

00:14:17.156 --> 00:14:19.750
"Faster than light,
no left or right."

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:22.851
When possible,
maintain a linear trajectory.

00:14:22.928 --> 00:14:25.294
Course corrections
could fracture the hull.

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:27.491
Exactly. We'd have
to drop to impulse

00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:29.625
every time we made
a course change,

00:14:29.702 --> 00:14:32.296
but what if we let
Voyager do the driving?

00:14:32.371 --> 00:14:34.168
Ma'am?

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.935
We could preprogram
every kilometer.

00:14:36.008 --> 00:14:38.476
That way we'd only spend
a second or two at impulse

00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:40.444
every time the computer
executed a turn.

00:14:40.512 --> 00:14:41.945
Auto-navigation
the entire way?

00:14:42.047 --> 00:14:43.776
No offense,
but the neural gel packs

00:14:43.849 --> 00:14:46.784
can calculate vectors
a little faster than you can.

00:14:46.852 --> 00:14:47.944
B'Elanna?

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:49.487
We'd need a more accurate

00:14:49.555 --> 00:14:50.852
scan of the region.

00:14:50.923 --> 00:14:53.221
If we even graze
one of those vacuoles...

00:14:53.292 --> 00:14:55.089
We could send
a shuttle ahead.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.149
The Delta Flyer.

00:14:56.228 --> 00:14:58.958
Its sensors
are more advanced.

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:03.032
The Delta what?

00:15:05.237 --> 00:15:06.829
Forgive me.

00:15:06.906 --> 00:15:09.534
I... must have been thinking
of another starship.

00:15:10.609 --> 00:15:12.509
Prepare a shuttle.

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.375
I want all
of Voyager's systems

00:15:14.446 --> 00:15:17.279
operating at peak efficiency
by the time Tom gets back.

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:18.816
If we're going
to pull this off,

00:15:18.884 --> 00:15:21.182
there's no margin
for error. Dismissed.

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:38.536
Computer, display an image
of the Ocampan homeworld.

00:15:42.374 --> 00:15:45.275
Plot a course
from Voyager's current position.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:51.681
Homesick?

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.718
Lieutenant.

00:15:53.786 --> 00:15:56.084
Tom.

00:15:56.155 --> 00:15:57.281
It's okay.

00:15:57.356 --> 00:15:59.483
A lot of people on
board feel the same way.

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:03.517
I spent my entire life trying
to get away from Ocampa.

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:05.586
Why would I want
to go back?

00:16:05.664 --> 00:16:06.995
Because it's home.

00:16:07.066 --> 00:16:09.660
Home for me means
a penal colony.

00:16:09.735 --> 00:16:13.466
Out here, I get to fly
a state-of-the-art ship,

00:16:13.539 --> 00:16:16.167
and there's no admirals
in sight.

00:16:16.241 --> 00:16:17.333
What are you doing?

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:20.378
Getting ready
for a scouting mission.

00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:26.011
You planning on going somewhere?

00:16:26.085 --> 00:16:27.916
Uh, no, of course not.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:31.786
I was just studying
the helm configurations.

00:16:31.857 --> 00:16:34.883
I didn't know
you could pilot a shuttle.

00:16:36.161 --> 00:16:37.253
I can't...

00:16:37.329 --> 00:16:39.126
but I'd like to learn.

00:16:39.198 --> 00:16:41.257
Well, then,
why not learn from the best?

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:43.062
I could start you off
on the holodeck

00:16:43.135 --> 00:16:44.466
on an old class-1.

00:16:44.536 --> 00:16:47.437
That's the kind of shuttle
my father used to take me up in.

00:16:47.506 --> 00:16:49.940
That would be
very nice, Lieutenant.

00:16:51.777 --> 00:16:53.039
Tom.

00:17:04.656 --> 00:17:07.124
Identify yourself.

00:17:07.192 --> 00:17:08.420
It's me, Tuvok.

00:17:08.494 --> 00:17:09.791
Naomi Wildman.

00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:42.159
May I help you, sir?

00:17:42.227 --> 00:17:44.627
Lieutenant, is
something wrong?

00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:04.873
Hello, sweeting.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:09.182
I took the liberty of preparing
one of your favorite meals.

00:18:09.254 --> 00:18:12.314
It's under replicator program
"Neelix 1."

00:18:12.391 --> 00:18:14.882
Call me
if you'd like some company.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.291
Miss you.

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:22.892
Computer, end music.

00:18:23.035 --> 00:18:24.900
Open an encrypted channel.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.565
Direct the signal
to the following coordinates.

00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:35.178
Channel open.

00:18:35.247 --> 00:18:36.236
My name is Kes.

00:18:36.315 --> 00:18:37.782
I'm aboard the Starship Voyager.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:38.817
Respond.

00:18:40.552 --> 00:18:43.112
I know you're receiving
this transmission,

00:18:43.188 --> 00:18:45.213
and I also know
that your attempt

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.258
to capture this ship will fail.

00:18:47.326 --> 00:18:49.658
If you want
to harvest Voyager's crew,

00:18:49.728 --> 00:18:51.787
I suggest you answer me now.

00:18:54.433 --> 00:18:55.593
Explain.

00:18:55.667 --> 00:18:58.397
Captain Janeway is aware
of your ambush.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.064
She's found a way
to evade your vessels,

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.573
but I can help you.

00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:04.836
I'm listening.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.036
I can send you

00:19:06.111 --> 00:19:07.703
tactical data
on their shields, weapons...

00:19:07.779 --> 00:19:10.213
everything you need
to take this ship.

00:19:10.282 --> 00:19:12.409
This is a deception.

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:14.679
Do you want this crew or not?

00:19:14.753 --> 00:19:17.620
In return?

00:19:17.689 --> 00:19:21.420
Safe passage to Ocampa
for myself and one other.

00:19:21.493 --> 00:19:24.894
Why would you sentence
your own crew to death?

00:19:24.963 --> 00:19:26.658
They're not my crew.

00:19:26.732 --> 00:19:29.530
They abandoned me
a long time ago.

00:20:08.273 --> 00:20:11.037
Computer, access Voyager's
tactical database.

00:20:11.109 --> 00:20:14.101
Command authorization required.

00:20:17.449 --> 00:20:19.644
Access granted.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.813
Naomi Wildman?

00:20:23.889 --> 00:20:27.290
She appeared to be
half Ktarian.

00:20:27.359 --> 00:20:29.088
Ensign Wildman's
husband is Ktarian.

00:20:29.161 --> 00:20:30.822
I met him once on
Deep Space 9.

00:20:30.896 --> 00:20:31.954
There's more.

00:20:32.064 --> 00:20:34.794
I followed her to Cargo Bay 2,

00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:37.960
where I saw a woman
and two children,

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.630
all with cybernetic implants.

00:20:40.706 --> 00:20:42.640
Borg?

00:20:42.708 --> 00:20:44.938
I can't explain
it, Captain.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:48.844
I've had hallucinations
before, but only while

00:20:48.914 --> 00:20:51.348
in a state of
deep meditation.

00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:53.350
These were specific,

00:20:53.418 --> 00:20:56.854
and they evoked a
sense of anticipation.

00:20:56.922 --> 00:20:59.220
It almost sounds like
you're describing a premonition.

00:20:59.291 --> 00:21:00.724
Indeed.

00:21:00.792 --> 00:21:03.158
I didn't think
Vulcans had premonitions.

00:21:03.228 --> 00:21:04.354
They don't.

00:21:04.429 --> 00:21:06.989
That's what concerns me.

00:21:09.167 --> 00:21:12.728
Computer, maintain
a continuous proximity scan

00:21:12.804 --> 00:21:14.169
of Lieutenant Tuvok,

00:21:14.239 --> 00:21:17.140
ten meter radius,
all sensor parameters.

00:21:17.209 --> 00:21:19.177
In case you have
any more "visions."

00:21:19.244 --> 00:21:21.872
A logical plan.

00:21:21.947 --> 00:21:23.244
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:21:23.315 --> 00:21:24.282
Go ahead.

00:21:24.349 --> 00:21:25.611
We're approaching the vacuoles.

00:21:25.684 --> 00:21:26.651
On my way.

00:21:39.264 --> 00:21:41.789
Last chance to take
the long way around.

00:21:41.867 --> 00:21:44.427
It does feel like
we're sneaking through

00:21:44.503 --> 00:21:45.492
a graveyard at midnight.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.730
Any sign of the Vidiians?

00:21:46.805 --> 00:21:49.968
Not yet, but it's a safe
bet they're in there.

00:21:50.108 --> 00:21:50.972
Tom?

00:21:51.109 --> 00:21:52.838
Trajectories
laid in.

00:21:52.911 --> 00:21:57.177
Our trip will take three hours,
12 minutes, 11 seconds,

00:21:57.249 --> 00:21:59.183
with 216 course changes.

00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:01.617
Well, let's get started.

00:22:01.687 --> 00:22:03.917
Engaging at warp 8.

00:22:04.056 --> 00:22:06.889
Sit back and enjoy the ride.

00:22:10.329 --> 00:22:12.763
One of the vacuoles
shifted position.

00:22:12.831 --> 00:22:14.594
The computer's
adjusting our vector.

00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:17.567
Dropping to impulse.

00:22:17.636 --> 00:22:20.036
2.3 degree turn starboard.

00:22:20.105 --> 00:22:21.936
Jumping to warp 6.

00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:23.201
One down,

00:22:23.275 --> 00:22:24.606
215 to go.

00:22:24.676 --> 00:22:26.871
I'll be in Sick Bay.

00:22:28.747 --> 00:22:31.307
Dropping to impulse.

00:22:31.383 --> 00:22:33.544
New heading: O-31 mark 2.

00:22:35.887 --> 00:22:37.548
There's a ship approaching.

00:22:37.622 --> 00:22:39.180
It's on a collision course.

00:22:39.257 --> 00:22:41.589
I'm not reading any ship.

00:22:43.995 --> 00:22:45.257
Lieutenant?

00:22:52.471 --> 00:22:56.066
Permission to be relieved, sir.

00:22:56.141 --> 00:22:58.439
I am not well.

00:22:58.510 --> 00:23:00.478
Of course.

00:23:10.088 --> 00:23:13.285
The molecular structures
appear to be stable. Good.

00:23:15.727 --> 00:23:16.751
Report.

00:23:16.828 --> 00:23:18.056
We've devised a neural agent

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:20.325
that should inhibit the
Vidiians' motor functions

00:23:20.399 --> 00:23:22.060
without causing any
permanent damage.

00:23:22.134 --> 00:23:24.466
Good. I don't want to add
to their health problems.

00:23:24.536 --> 00:23:26.629
I just want to keep them
from adding to ours.

00:23:26.705 --> 00:23:28.263
I'll get to work.

00:23:32.744 --> 00:23:33.836
Doctor...

00:23:33.912 --> 00:23:35.174
when was the last time

00:23:35.247 --> 00:23:37.681
you examined
Ensign Wildman?

00:23:37.749 --> 00:23:41.344
I performed her annual physical
six weeks ago.

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:44.082
Did you find anything unusual?

00:23:44.156 --> 00:23:46.716
She's in perfect health.

00:23:46.792 --> 00:23:49.260
This may seem like
a strange question,

00:23:49.327 --> 00:23:51.795
but I need to know
if she's pregnant.

00:23:51.863 --> 00:23:54.923
I'm not at liberty to
disclose that information.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.968
Doctor-patient
confidentiality.

00:23:57.035 --> 00:23:58.969
What about "Captain's orders?"

00:23:59.037 --> 00:23:59.969
Sorry.

00:24:00.038 --> 00:24:01.198
Medical protocol supersede

00:24:01.273 --> 00:24:02.706
your authority
in these matters.

00:24:02.774 --> 00:24:05.766
The security of this ship
could be at stake.

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.780
She planned on
telling you herself.

00:24:10.849 --> 00:24:11.907
Boy or girl?

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:13.847
Female... half Ktarian,
as a matter of fact,

00:24:13.919 --> 00:24:15.079
which should
nearly double

00:24:15.153 --> 00:24:16.586
the infant's gestation period.

00:24:16.655 --> 00:24:17.781
How did you know?

00:24:21.326 --> 00:24:24.159
And they say I'm rude.

00:24:24.229 --> 00:24:26.288
We're receiving a distress call.

00:24:26.364 --> 00:24:28.195
Life signs?

00:24:28.266 --> 00:24:29.858
It's Ocampan.

00:24:29.935 --> 00:24:31.266
Kes?

00:24:31.336 --> 00:24:32.496
Let me come on board.

00:24:32.571 --> 00:24:34.095
Her ship is accelerating.

00:24:34.172 --> 00:24:35.935
It's on a collision course.

00:24:36.007 --> 00:24:37.941
Hull breach on Deck 9!

00:24:38.009 --> 00:24:39.340
Emergency force fields.

00:24:39.411 --> 00:24:41.208
She's approaching
Main Engineering.

00:24:41.279 --> 00:24:42.576
State your intentions.

00:24:42.647 --> 00:24:43.909
Let me come on board.

00:24:43.982 --> 00:24:45.074
It's on a collision course.

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:46.549
We're receiving
a distress call.

00:24:46.618 --> 00:24:48.210
Bridge to Engineering.
Intruder alert.

00:24:48.286 --> 00:24:49.218
Stop where you are.

00:24:49.287 --> 00:24:50.219
Kes?

00:24:50.288 --> 00:24:51.220
State your intentions.

00:24:51.289 --> 00:24:52.221
Warp power's fluctuating.

00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:53.257
Torres to Bridge.

00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:54.349
Kes is in direct contact
with the warp core.

00:24:54.426 --> 00:24:55.552
She's drawing power
from it somehow.

00:24:55.627 --> 00:24:56.594
Shut it down!

00:24:57.629 --> 00:24:59.688
Problem?

00:25:13.044 --> 00:25:14.341
Hey.

00:25:16.982 --> 00:25:18.643
Torres to Sick Bay.

00:25:18.717 --> 00:25:20.378
Medical emergency.

00:25:21.653 --> 00:25:23.416
20 milligrams lectrazine.

00:25:26.057 --> 00:25:28.082
Cortical stimulator.

00:25:33.832 --> 00:25:35.129
We'll start at 20 millijoules.

00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:36.189
- Ready.
- Now!

00:25:38.203 --> 00:25:41.195
He's gone into synaptic shock.

00:25:41.273 --> 00:25:43.264
I don't understand.

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:52.780
Can I speak with him?

00:25:52.851 --> 00:25:55.285
I think it's best to keep him
sedated for now.

00:25:55.353 --> 00:25:57.287
When did this begin?

00:25:57.355 --> 00:25:59.152
Earlier this afternoon
in Engineering.

00:25:59.224 --> 00:26:01.715
Time... I need the exact time.

00:26:01.793 --> 00:26:06.287
Lieutenant Torres called
Sick Bay at 1422 hours.

00:26:09.668 --> 00:26:11.898
Computer, display proximity scan
of Lieutenant Tuvok

00:26:12.003 --> 00:26:15.461
at 1422 hours.

00:26:18.076 --> 00:26:19.100
Oh...

00:26:19.177 --> 00:26:20.701
Captain?

00:26:20.779 --> 00:26:22.804
Tachyons.

00:26:22.881 --> 00:26:24.041
I beg your pardon?

00:26:24.115 --> 00:26:26.208
There was a surge
of tachyon particles

00:26:26.284 --> 00:26:27.717
just before Tuvok collapsed.

00:26:27.786 --> 00:26:29.720
That could have triggered this,

00:26:29.788 --> 00:26:31.585
but where did they come from?

00:26:31.656 --> 00:26:34.625
They're normally caused
by temporal distortions.

00:26:34.693 --> 00:26:35.717
Time travel?

00:26:35.794 --> 00:26:38.058
Let me know
if his condition changes.

00:26:41.199 --> 00:26:42.598
Kes...

00:26:42.667 --> 00:26:45.534
you have telepathic abilities.

00:26:45.604 --> 00:26:49.199
Have you experienced
anything unusual

00:26:49.274 --> 00:26:52.266
during the past couple of days?

00:26:52.344 --> 00:26:55.142
Hallucinations, premonitions?

00:26:55.213 --> 00:26:56.305
No, nothing.

00:26:56.381 --> 00:26:59.214
If you do, you'll let me know?

00:26:59.284 --> 00:27:01.479
Of course, Captain.

00:27:11.062 --> 00:27:13.223
We're low on neuro-stabilizers.

00:27:13.298 --> 00:27:15.391
I'll go replicate some more.

00:27:17.202 --> 00:27:19.227
Hurry back.

00:27:19.304 --> 00:27:21.101
Where's the tactical data
you promised us?

00:27:21.172 --> 00:27:22.366
I'm downloading it now.

00:27:22.440 --> 00:27:24.772
I'll transmit it to you
once you've arrived.

00:27:24.843 --> 00:27:26.674
I need it now!

00:27:26.745 --> 00:27:28.372
Janeway's already suspicious.

00:27:28.446 --> 00:27:30.778
If I transmit it now,
I'll be discovered.

00:27:30.849 --> 00:27:32.373
That's your problem.

00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:34.384
Apparently it's yours, too.

00:27:39.658 --> 00:27:42.923
Gentlemen, scan for
tachyon particles deck by deck.

00:27:42.994 --> 00:27:43.926
Tachyons?

00:27:43.995 --> 00:27:44.927
Do it.

00:27:44.996 --> 00:27:46.930
Looking for something specific?

00:27:46.998 --> 00:27:48.124
I'm not sure.

00:27:50.502 --> 00:27:51.469
Report!

00:27:51.536 --> 00:27:52.935
We're under attack.

00:27:53.004 --> 00:27:54.938
A Vidiian ship is closing
on our position.

00:27:55.006 --> 00:27:56.997
Battle stations.

00:28:13.191 --> 00:28:15.785
We've lost warp drive
and weapons.

00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:17.384
They're cutting
through our shields.

00:28:17.462 --> 00:28:18.724
Remodulate.

00:28:18.797 --> 00:28:20.059
I'm trying.

00:28:20.131 --> 00:28:22.065
They keep matching
the frequencies.

00:28:22.133 --> 00:28:23.464
We've still got impulse.

00:28:23.535 --> 00:28:25.366
They've taken out navigation.

00:28:25.437 --> 00:28:26.927
I can't plot a course.

00:28:45.490 --> 00:28:48.084
They're cutting an access route
through the hull.

00:28:48.159 --> 00:28:50.059
Evacuate Deck 3 and seal it off.

00:28:50.128 --> 00:28:51.220
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:28:51.296 --> 00:28:52.923
Are you ready
with that neural agent?

00:28:53.031 --> 00:28:54.157
Aye, Captain.

00:28:54.232 --> 00:28:55.790
Stand by to release it
on Deck 3.

00:28:55.867 --> 00:28:57.129
Acknowledged.

00:28:57.202 --> 00:28:58.897
50 milliliters should suffice.

00:29:00.438 --> 00:29:01.871
Doctor!

00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:03.202
Doctor to the Bridge.

00:29:03.274 --> 00:29:05.299
Environmental controls
aren't responding!

00:29:05.376 --> 00:29:06.843
Harry, what's going on?

00:29:06.911 --> 00:29:09.311
We've been locked out
of that system.

00:29:09.380 --> 00:29:11.348
What do you mean, "locked out?"

00:29:11.416 --> 00:29:13.646
The command relays
have been fused.

00:29:13.718 --> 00:29:15.413
They knew where to find us.

00:29:15.487 --> 00:29:17.512
They knew our
shield frequencies,

00:29:17.589 --> 00:29:19.216
which systems to target...

00:29:19.290 --> 00:29:20.882
We're being boarded!

00:29:20.959 --> 00:29:22.654
I'm reading an EM fluctuation.

00:29:22.727 --> 00:29:24.319
It could be a transmission.

00:29:24.395 --> 00:29:25.293
Location?

00:29:25.363 --> 00:29:27.354
Airponics Bay.

00:29:27.432 --> 00:29:28.364
Who's down there?

00:29:28.433 --> 00:29:30.560
I'm picking up two bio-readings.

00:29:30.635 --> 00:29:33.160
The sensors must
be malfunctioning.

00:29:33.238 --> 00:29:34.865
They're both reading as Kes.

00:29:35.940 --> 00:29:38.340
Security to Airponics Bay.

00:29:38.409 --> 00:29:40.400
Shut down control functions
to that section.

00:29:40.478 --> 00:29:42.036
I'm going down there.

00:29:42.113 --> 00:29:43.842
Something tells me
we've got more

00:29:43.915 --> 00:29:45.473
than one battle on our hands.

00:29:56.494 --> 00:29:59.395
Computer, initiate
site-to-site transport.

00:29:59.464 --> 00:30:00.931
Program Kes beta-6.

00:30:00.999 --> 00:30:02.489
Unable to comply.

00:30:02.567 --> 00:30:04.762
Control functions
have been disabled.

00:30:13.344 --> 00:30:14.777
Shh! Shh!

00:30:14.846 --> 00:30:16.814
Shh. I'm taking you home.

00:30:34.966 --> 00:30:36.558
We've got weapons back.

00:30:36.634 --> 00:30:37.965
Can you target those hooks?

00:30:38.036 --> 00:30:39.298
Not at this range.

00:30:39.370 --> 00:30:40.632
We'd breach the upper hull.

00:30:40.705 --> 00:30:42.400
It's better than
being dissected.

00:30:44.275 --> 00:30:46.209
Reverse the hull polarity.

00:30:46.277 --> 00:30:48.472
Maybe we can shake them loose.

00:30:55.820 --> 00:30:57.845
Now, one of you
doesn't belong here,

00:30:57.922 --> 00:31:01.756
and I'm guessing it's you.

00:31:01.826 --> 00:31:05.125
Tuvok's premonitions were real.

00:31:05.196 --> 00:31:07.630
You're from the future.

00:31:07.699 --> 00:31:10.429
A future I'm about to change.

00:31:10.501 --> 00:31:13.561
You're helping
the Vidiians, Kes.

00:31:13.638 --> 00:31:15.105
Why?

00:31:24.215 --> 00:31:26.615
...Security to Deck 11...

00:31:32.657 --> 00:31:35.524
Tell me why you're doing this.

00:31:35.593 --> 00:31:37.151
I won't let you hurt her again.

00:31:37.228 --> 00:31:38.889
I haven't done anything
to harm her.

00:31:38.963 --> 00:31:40.328
You took her from Ocampa...

00:31:40.398 --> 00:31:41.865
her home.

00:31:41.933 --> 00:31:43.662
She's a prisoner on this ship.

00:31:43.735 --> 00:31:46.260
No one's a prisoner here, Kes.

00:31:46.337 --> 00:31:47.599
I was a child.

00:31:47.672 --> 00:31:49.435
You corrupted me
with your ideas.

00:31:49.507 --> 00:31:50.769
What ideas?

00:31:50.842 --> 00:31:52.707
Exploration, discovery.

00:31:52.777 --> 00:31:54.142
I believed you!

00:31:56.281 --> 00:31:57.873
Hull polarity
loosened their hold

00:31:57.949 --> 00:31:58.973
but not by much.

00:31:59.117 --> 00:32:00.379
It's a start.

00:32:00.451 --> 00:32:01.748
Reroute the deflector.

00:32:01.819 --> 00:32:04.049
Have it discharge
antigraviton pulses

00:32:04.122 --> 00:32:05.384
along the hull.

00:32:05.456 --> 00:32:07.424
Engage the inertial dampers.

00:32:07.492 --> 00:32:09.653
Get a controlled pitch going.

00:32:13.731 --> 00:32:15.790
In three years, I'm
going to leave Voyager

00:32:15.867 --> 00:32:17.266
in search of higher things,

00:32:17.335 --> 00:32:19.132
because you encouraged me
to do it.

00:32:19.203 --> 00:32:20.465
You encouraged me

00:32:20.538 --> 00:32:22.506
to develop my mental abilities.

00:32:22.573 --> 00:32:23.835
I wasn't ready.

00:32:23.908 --> 00:32:27.901
But what I found...
I couldn't control it.

00:32:27.979 --> 00:32:29.913
It scared me.

00:32:29.981 --> 00:32:31.949
I had nowhere to go.

00:32:32.016 --> 00:32:35.213
I thought of returning
home to Ocampa,

00:32:35.286 --> 00:32:37.345
but I had changed too much.

00:32:37.422 --> 00:32:39.947
I knew
they'd be frightened of me.

00:32:40.058 --> 00:32:44.324
I knew they wouldn't accept me,
but they'll accept her.

00:32:44.395 --> 00:32:46.386
You don't have
to destroy this ship, Kes.

00:32:46.464 --> 00:32:47.726
We can help you.

00:32:47.799 --> 00:32:50.233
No. I trusted you.

00:32:50.301 --> 00:32:51.233
Kes...

00:32:51.302 --> 00:32:52.633
No!

00:33:00.078 --> 00:33:01.306
We're breaking free!

00:33:01.379 --> 00:33:02.607
They're trying

00:33:02.680 --> 00:33:04.147
to lock on us
with a tractor beam.

00:33:04.215 --> 00:33:05.477
Reverse thrusters.

00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:06.812
Full power.

00:33:06.884 --> 00:33:08.317
That could tear
the hull apart.

00:33:08.386 --> 00:33:09.683
Then tear it apart!

00:33:21.766 --> 00:33:23.893
Photon torpedoes... full spread.

00:33:24.936 --> 00:33:26.801
Ready!

00:33:26.871 --> 00:33:28.600
Fire!

00:33:49.994 --> 00:33:51.894
It's set to kill, Kes.

00:34:20.491 --> 00:34:21.924
Janeway to Bridge.

00:34:21.993 --> 00:34:23.426
Status?

00:34:23.494 --> 00:34:25.553
The Vidiians are in retreat.

00:34:25.630 --> 00:34:28.929
Everything all right down there?

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.831
For now.

00:34:51.789 --> 00:34:53.814
She was here...

00:34:53.891 --> 00:34:57.224
in my last premonition.

00:34:57.295 --> 00:35:00.196
She appeared older.

00:35:00.264 --> 00:35:02.391
Her face was tired.

00:35:02.467 --> 00:35:04.526
What was she doing?

00:35:04.602 --> 00:35:07.662
She had her hands
on the casing,

00:35:07.738 --> 00:35:10.639
as if she was drawing
energy from it.

00:35:10.708 --> 00:35:13.871
The tachyons
are concentrated here.

00:35:13.945 --> 00:35:15.879
It's possible
she needed the core

00:35:15.947 --> 00:35:18.211
to travel back in time.

00:35:18.282 --> 00:35:22.582
If that's true, then
she'll need it again.

00:35:22.653 --> 00:35:25.918
But we don't know
when that'll be.

00:35:25.990 --> 00:35:27.548
We have to be ready.

00:35:27.625 --> 00:35:29.149
Doctor to the Captain.

00:35:29.227 --> 00:35:30.251
Go ahead.

00:35:30.328 --> 00:35:32.728
Kes has regained consciousness.

00:35:34.132 --> 00:35:35.929
What do you remember?

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.262
I was in Airponics,

00:35:37.335 --> 00:35:38.393
and then I felt dizzy,

00:35:38.469 --> 00:35:40.096
and then I was watching myself.

00:35:40.171 --> 00:35:41.399
Yourself?

00:35:41.472 --> 00:35:43.599
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:35:47.778 --> 00:35:49.211
What I'm about to tell you

00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.941
stays between the three of us.

00:35:51.048 --> 00:35:52.106
Understood?

00:35:52.183 --> 00:35:54.378
Yes, Captain.

00:35:54.452 --> 00:35:56.943
Something terrible
has happened...

00:35:57.088 --> 00:35:59.454
or, more precisely, will happen.

00:35:59.524 --> 00:36:00.821
We're going to need your help

00:36:00.892 --> 00:36:02.553
to prevent it
from happening again.

00:36:16.541 --> 00:36:19.271
It took exhaustive research

00:36:19.343 --> 00:36:22.710
sifting through
teraquads of data,

00:36:22.780 --> 00:36:25.510
separating fact from rumor...

00:36:25.583 --> 00:36:28.381
but eventually,
I arrived at the truth.

00:36:29.453 --> 00:36:31.478
Captain...

00:36:37.962 --> 00:36:40.123
Happy Birthday.

00:36:40.198 --> 00:36:42.098
Thank you.

00:36:42.166 --> 00:36:43.929
So, it's not long
before you hit

00:36:44.001 --> 00:36:45.730
the big three digits, huh?

00:36:45.803 --> 00:36:47.236
Indeed.

00:36:47.305 --> 00:36:50.138
Have you informed
anyone else of your discovery?

00:36:50.208 --> 00:36:52.438
Don't worry, Tuvok,
my lips are sealed.

00:36:52.510 --> 00:36:55.172
Well, you're supposed
to blow out the candle.

00:36:55.246 --> 00:36:57.146
That is not a Vulcan custom.

00:36:57.215 --> 00:36:59.308
Humor me.

00:36:59.383 --> 00:37:00.748
Captain to the Bridge.

00:37:00.818 --> 00:37:03.378
On my way.

00:37:03.454 --> 00:37:05.217
Well?

00:37:09.994 --> 00:37:11.859
It was a fire hazard.

00:37:19.403 --> 00:37:21.371
We're receiving
a distress call...

00:37:21.439 --> 00:37:23.839
a small vessel on
an intercept course.

00:37:23.908 --> 00:37:25.136
Life signs?

00:37:25.209 --> 00:37:26.267
One.

00:37:26.344 --> 00:37:28.335
It's Ocampan.

00:37:34.752 --> 00:37:36.811
I'd almost forgotten.

00:37:38.789 --> 00:37:40.222
We're being hailed.

00:37:40.291 --> 00:37:42.418
Red Alert.

00:37:42.493 --> 00:37:44.188
Raise shields.

00:37:44.262 --> 00:37:45.524
Captain?

00:37:45.596 --> 00:37:47.359
All hands, this is the Bridge.

00:37:47.431 --> 00:37:49.729
Begin emergency
evacuation of Deck 11.

00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:51.233
Repeat:

00:37:51.302 --> 00:37:53.600
All hands evacuate Deck 11.

00:37:53.671 --> 00:37:55.696
You heard her. Get moving!

00:37:58.142 --> 00:37:59.268
Now!

00:38:00.578 --> 00:38:02.011
Open a channel.

00:38:06.817 --> 00:38:08.546
Kes.

00:38:08.619 --> 00:38:11.417
Captain Janeway...

00:38:11.489 --> 00:38:13.480
I need your help.

00:38:13.557 --> 00:38:16.993
Will you please give me
permission to come aboard?

00:38:17.061 --> 00:38:19.427
Of course. What's happened?

00:38:19.497 --> 00:38:21.624
Please, let me come aboard.

00:38:25.503 --> 00:38:26.731
Her ship is accelerating.

00:38:26.804 --> 00:38:28.169
It's on a collision course.

00:38:28.239 --> 00:38:30.173
Five seconds to impact.

00:38:30.241 --> 00:38:31.105
Tuvok.

00:38:31.175 --> 00:38:33.166
Lock on a tractor beam.

00:38:33.244 --> 00:38:35.212
Evasive maneuvers.

00:38:36.247 --> 00:38:37.908
Shields are holding.

00:38:37.982 --> 00:38:39.609
Her ship is intact.

00:38:39.684 --> 00:38:40.616
Captain, a transporter

00:38:40.685 --> 00:38:42.118
was activated
just before impact.

00:38:42.186 --> 00:38:43.448
She's beamed aboard.

00:38:48.459 --> 00:38:50.757
I'm reading bulkhead ruptures
on Deck 11,

00:38:50.828 --> 00:38:53.262
Section 17... 18, 19.

00:38:53.331 --> 00:38:55.629
How did you know?

00:38:57.368 --> 00:38:58.699
Ready?

00:38:59.804 --> 00:39:01.931
Shut down the warp core.

00:39:02.006 --> 00:39:03.997
You have the Bridge.

00:39:27.131 --> 00:39:29.065
Remember me?

00:39:29.133 --> 00:39:31.727
The innocent child
you're here to save?

00:39:31.802 --> 00:39:34.794
You blame Captain Janeway,

00:39:34.872 --> 00:39:36.635
but the choice was yours.

00:39:36.707 --> 00:39:39.676
You made the decision
to leave Ocampa,

00:39:39.744 --> 00:39:43.180
and you made the decision
to leave Voyager.

00:39:43.247 --> 00:39:46.444
If you're watching me now,
you've come back to take revenge

00:39:46.517 --> 00:39:48.610
on the people
who cared about you.

00:39:48.686 --> 00:39:51.211
That's not who you are,
and that's not who I am.

00:39:51.288 --> 00:39:52.550
Don't do this.

00:39:52.623 --> 00:39:53.715
Find another way home.

00:39:53.791 --> 00:39:55.315
Captain Janeway will help you

00:39:55.393 --> 00:39:57.918
if you give her a chance.

00:39:58.028 --> 00:40:00.519
Try to remember who you were.

00:40:00.598 --> 00:40:02.361
Try to remember me.

00:40:05.336 --> 00:40:07.930
Don't you remember?

00:40:08.072 --> 00:40:10.199
You made that holo-recording,

00:40:10.274 --> 00:40:13.209
because you didn't want
this to happen again.

00:40:13.277 --> 00:40:17.941
Three years ago,
you traveled back in time.

00:40:18.082 --> 00:40:21.609
Kes, you wanted to take
that woman with you,

00:40:21.685 --> 00:40:23.482
and you were willing

00:40:23.554 --> 00:40:26.148
to hand the rest of us over
to the Vidiians to do it.

00:40:26.223 --> 00:40:27.952
It didn't work.

00:40:28.058 --> 00:40:30.322
You forced me to kill you, Kes.

00:40:30.394 --> 00:40:33.795
If you go back now,
it'll all happen again.

00:40:35.533 --> 00:40:38.297
Just before this
terrible thing happened,

00:40:38.369 --> 00:40:40.667
you told me
you had nowhere to go.

00:40:40.738 --> 00:40:42.433
That's not true.

00:40:42.506 --> 00:40:43.973
Stay here with us.

00:40:44.041 --> 00:40:45.338
I can't.

00:40:45.409 --> 00:40:46.842
I don't belong here.

00:40:46.911 --> 00:40:49.311
I need to be with
my own people.

00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:51.848
You told me you had
the ability to get home,

00:40:51.916 --> 00:40:54.783
but you were afraid the Ocampans
wouldn't accept you.

00:40:54.852 --> 00:40:56.046
Why?

00:41:02.960 --> 00:41:04.655
I remember...

00:41:04.728 --> 00:41:07.891
What? What do you remember?

00:41:07.965 --> 00:41:10.365
The holo-recording...
I remember making it.

00:41:10.434 --> 00:41:13.301
You asked me to help
you to help myself.

00:41:16.907 --> 00:41:20.502
You wanted me to
remember who I was.

00:41:22.379 --> 00:41:25.974
These years were so
filled with confusion...

00:41:29.153 --> 00:41:32.179
and anger. I...

00:41:32.256 --> 00:41:35.953
I buried the memory.

00:41:36.093 --> 00:41:38.220
I'd almost forgotten.

00:41:44.969 --> 00:41:48.405
Does it really matter
which Kes goes home?

00:41:54.278 --> 00:41:56.803
A few snacks
for the journey home.

00:41:56.881 --> 00:42:00.476
You do still like leola root?

00:42:00.551 --> 00:42:02.485
Thank you.

00:42:05.155 --> 00:42:07.248
What?

00:42:07.324 --> 00:42:10.259
Just looking.

00:42:10.327 --> 00:42:12.420
See anyone you know?

00:42:13.797 --> 00:42:15.389
Only you.

00:42:24.308 --> 00:42:25.570
Good-bye, Kes.

00:42:25.643 --> 00:42:27.907
Captain.

00:42:44.895 --> 00:42:48.058
What should we tell the others?

00:42:48.132 --> 00:42:51.329
A friend got lost.

00:42:51.402 --> 00:42:54.371
We helped her find her way.
